Report DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR for shared GBM resources with an implicit modifier

vrend allocates every resource the guest can ask about through the GBM layout
query (VIRGL_CCMD_GET_PIPE_RESOURCE_LAYOUT, only issued for VIRGL_BIND_SHARED)
with GBM_BO_USE_LINEAR forced, because the virtio-gpu kernel driver supports no
other modifier. The host driver still reports DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID for a
surface it created without an explicit modifier (radeonsi reports INVALID for
both its linear and its tiled surfaces), so the guest was told the buffer is
linear in stride but "implicitly tiled" in modifier.

A guest that exports such a resource as a dma-buf (Chromium's cursor and
scanout buffers, via gbm_bo_get_modifier) then hands waypipe/venus an INVALID
modifier, which is not a member of any device's modifier list: venus rejects the
import with "unsupported modifier", and the waypipe server turns that into a
wl_display error that kills the client's GPU process.

The buffer really is linear, so report the linear modifier for the resources
vrend forced to GBM_BO_USE_LINEAR. Gated on VIRGL_BIND_SHARED on purpose: for
any other bind the modifier says nothing about the tiling.

--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -13749,6 +13749,16 @@
       layout.num_planes = num_planes;
       layout.modifier = gbm_bo_get_modifier(res->gbm_bo);
 
+      /* vrend allocates every shared resource with GBM_BO_USE_LINEAR because the
+       * virtio-gpu kernel driver supports no other modifier, but the host driver
+       * reports DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID for a surface it created without an
+       * explicit modifier. Report the linear modifier for those buffers, so a
+       * guest that exports the resource as a dma-buf hands out a usable
+       * (modifier, plane layout) pair instead of an unimportable INVALID one.
+       */
+      if (layout.modifier == DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID && (res->base.bind & VIRGL_BIND_SHARED))
+         layout.modifier = 0; /* DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR */
+
       for (uint32_t i = 0; i < layout.num_planes; i++) {
          layout.planes[i].offset = gbm_bo_get_offset(res->gbm_bo, i);
          layout.planes[i].stride = gbm_bo_get_stride_for_plane(res->gbm_bo, i);
